# A corrupt or hostile library in the plugin folder (cavekit-flash.md R10, T-580; PICKUP's "the in-daemon plugin scan is a
# landmine"). The fixture puts four into the shell's own plugin folder, the first the daemon searches, and drops the
# plugin registry so the folder is scanned: random bytes named .so, a library whose constructor never returns, one whose
# constructor aborts, one that is no plugin. The daemon reads each in a scanner process of its own under a 10 s limit
# (engine patch 0118): the page with the tone movie loads, the movie plays, navigator.plugins holds Flash and none of
# the four, and the daemon's log says what became of each.
id: flash-hostile-plugins
section: Flash
item: Four bad libraries in the plugin folder (random bytes, a constructor that never returns, one that aborts, one that is no plugin) leave the daemon serving: the page loads, Flash plays, and none of the four is a plugin
shells: enyo mochi mojo
fixture: hostile-plugins
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-flash-tone.html
kit: cavekit-flash.md R10
wait rect 'sel:embed' 40
expect audio audible 20
show-log 'plugin scan'
probe plugins '(function(){var a=[],bad=0;for(var i=0;i<navigator.plugins.length;i++){var f=navigator.plugins[i].filename;a.push(f);if(/jihad/.test(f))bad++;}return (bad?"HOSTILE ":"clean ")+a.join(" ");})()'
expect probe-has clean
expect probe-has libflashplayer.so
